# AERIS SITL baseline parameters.
#
# Format: one "NAME VALUE" pair per line, '#' starts a comment. Parsed by
# aeris.simulation.launcher.params.parse_params_file and applied over
# MAVLink PARAM_SET by aeris.simulation.launcher.params.apply_params.
#
# This is intentionally minimal for Phase 3 — it demonstrates the
# mechanism with one well-justified setting, not a general SITL tuning
# profile. Later phases add their own params (or their own profile that
# extends this one) rather than growing this file arbitrarily.

# COM_RC_IN_MODE=4 ("Disable manual control"): AERIS SITL has no RC
# transmitter and no MAVLink joystick — commanding comes entirely through
# MAVLink COMMAND_LONG / offboard setpoints. The PX4 default (3, "RC or
# MAVLink, keep first") is meant for a real vehicle with a real transmitter
# and is the standard community recommendation to change for a
# companion-computer-only setup. Source: PX4
# src/modules/commander/commander_params.c, read directly from the pinned
# checkout in Phase 3.
#
# UPDATE (Phase 4): the actual root cause of the Phase 1 arm-rejection
# finding was diagnosed and fixed in Phase 4 — PX4's health_and_arming_checks
# refuses to arm without a live GCS heartbeat on the link
# ("No connection to the GCS"), and Px4MavlinkAdapter didn't send one. See
# docs/phase_reports/phase-4.md and docs/vehicle.md. COM_RC_IN_MODE=4
# below was not the fix, but is kept — it remains independently
# well-justified for AERIS's RC-less, MAVLink-only SITL setup either way.
COM_RC_IN_MODE 4
